// src/std/core/loop/loop.zen
// the loop family's surface: nothing but starred re-exports.
//
// A folder root is a file of starred bindings and nothing else — the
// prefix earned the folder: three `loop_`-prefixed files with no root
// would leave every consumer importing the pieces, and every move
// inside the family breaking them.
//
// Range travels with the family because it's the family's parameter
// type, the same way str and String travel together — every
// loop_iter.zen signature names it. Declared in std.core.range, which
// answers "what is iterable", not "what is a loop": std.collections
// uses it as a plain index interval, never calling a loop word.

Range*               = std.core.range
LoopHandle*          = std.core.loop.loop_handle
loop*                = std.core.loop.loop_iter
// pairs is Map.pairs (collections_map.zen) — a member, not a free word
// here; see loop_iter.zen's closing note.
find*, filter*, map* = std.core.loop.loop_find
